g bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the test and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). The function's own description already said it used `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Now `2.665` rounds to `2.66` as the test expects, and `2.675` still rounds to `2.68`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I didn't merge it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}